From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Decode the image formats the web serves, within this device's
 memory

This ImageIO cannot decode WebP, so WebKit's own decoder does, and the formats
that cannot be decoded are no longer advertised to servers. The image size
query no longer recurses until the stack runs out, a size that is not known
yet is not divided by, an image is held before its observer is told about it,
the bytes an image arrived as are kept in a file rather than in dirty memory,
and purgeable decoded images stay off after measuring what they cost.
